dFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Stringent Response in </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr b="1" i="1" lang="en-US" sz="4000" u="none" cap="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>E. Coli</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:cxnSp><p:nvCxnSpPr><p:cNvPr id="492" name="Google Shape;492;p67"/><p:cNvCxnSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvCxnSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="304800" y="914400"/><a:ext cx="8382000" cy="0"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="straightConnector1"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln cap="flat" cmpd="thinThick" w="57150"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/><a:miter lim="800000"/><a:headEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/><a:tailEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="A diagram representing the stringent response in E. coli. A muffin-like structure is shown with a large yellow cap at the top and an orange base. The orange base opens up at the top, where two structures with yellow bulbs for a base, have a series of green strings looped and curved coming out of them. These are resting up into the bottom of the yellow cap of the structure, which is divided into three sections, labeled E on the left, P in the middle, and A at the right. The structure in the middle (in the P section) bonds up to a series of blue beads that curve up and left; the end of this structure is labeled, “Growing polypeptide,” and it has a NH3+ at its tip. The green structures with yellow bulbs rest on a green strand, which is labeled mRNA and 5’ on its left end, and curves up beneath the bulbed structures and then curved down right, where it is labeled 3’. The bottom of the orange part of the muffin structure sits on top of a blue base, labeled “Stringent factor (RelA protein).” A curved arrow points to the blue base away from GTP [plus] ATP, and a curved arrow points away from the blue base to (p)ppGpp [plus] AMP. Below (p)ppGpp is a dashed arrow that points down to a red circle with a red X in it, which sits on top of a purple mass with an opening to the right, labeled RNA polymerase. &#xA;" id="493" name="Google Shape;493;p67"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill rotWithShape="1"><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:srcRect b="0" l="0" r="0" t="0"/><a:stretch/></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="2574925" y="1095375"/><a:ext cx="4206875" cy="5600700"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>